# fir_scope in the emulator's window (ECP5_GUI_SCRIPT; see gui/src/trace.rs).
# The window runs this DSP-dense design at about 0.5 MHz, so a frame of two
# 4 Hz periods (12.5 million clocks) takes some 23 s here, and a 64 Hz frame
# about 1.5 s. Keys and buttons queue in the design's FIFO and act one per
# frame, so the presses come early and the script then lets the frames walk
# up the tone ladder. Buttons are held for a second: the design debounces
# them for 10 ms of board time.
0 rate max
0 run
1 board 3d
2 button 2 down    # FIRE2: noise high, a band of '.' around the clean '#'
3 button 2 up
5 button 3 down    # UP: 8 Hz
6 button 3 up
8 button 3 down    # UP: 16 Hz
9 button 3 up
11 button 3 down   # UP: 32 Hz
12 button 3 up
14 button 3 down   # UP: 64 Hz, the output shrinks
15 button 3 up
17 button 6 down   # RIGHT: filter 2, the ALU54B one, the same trace
18 button 6 up
85 quit
